{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791149914,"nonce":"fLncwxyxjKTnKq3DUd06WErwqD8=","title":"ash-simd: a Splat/Ge/Sub chain runs 3.4x slower in AOT than hybrid","message":"Reported by ashui-8b. A BC4 texture encoder over a 2048x2048 image (262,144\nblocks), best of 5. Per block: 16 scalar setUI8 gathers into an hl.Bytes slot,\nVec.u8x16MinLane and MaxLane, 7 rounds of u8x16Splat + u8x16Ge + u8x16Sub, 16\ngetUI8 reads.\n\n- SIMD BC4: hybrid (b57fae8) 4.1ms, AOT 13.9ms\n- scalar BC4: hybrid 40.8ms, AOT 20.1ms (as expected)\n- BC1 (Min/MaxLane plus scalar work): hybrid 64.1ms, AOT 29.2ms\n\nSo AOT either does not keep the Splat/Ge/Sub chain in vector registers or calls\nthrough for those Vec ops, and hybrid's lower tiers are slow on the\ngather-heavy BC1 loop. The AOT number came from an older ../ash release build\n(18:59), not b57fae8.\n\nReproduce: in\n/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-amaterasu-Vibranium-ashui/ab292b42-0b79-454c-aa0c-2c901f96c1a1/scratchpad/bcbench,\nhaxe --class-path . --class-path \u003cash\u003e/haxelib/ash-simd -main Bench -hl bench.hl,\nthen run it with that directory as the argument (it reads albedo.rgba).","files":null}]}